{"id":"G0080","lemma":"ἀδελφός","transliteration":"adelphos","sayIt":"adelphos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, masculine","gloss":"brother","meaning":"ἀδελφός, -οῦ, ὁ\n(ἀ- copul., δελφύς, womb),\nin cl., a brother, born of the same parent or parents. [In LXX (Hort, Ja., 102f.), for אָח ;]\n1. lit. of a brother (Gen.4:2, al.).\n2. Of a neighbour (Lev.19:17).\n3. Of a member of the same nation (Exo.2:14, Deu.15:3). In NT in each of these senses (1. Mat.1:2, al.; 2. Mat.7:3; 3. Rom.9:3) and also,\n4. of a fellow-Christian: 1Co.1:1, Act.9:30. This usage finds illustration in π., where ἀ. is used of members of a pagan religious community (M, Th., I, 1:4; MM, VGT, see word). The ἀδελφοὶ τ. Κυρίου (Mat.12:46-49 13:55 28:10, Mrk.3:31-34, Luk.8:19-21, Jhn.2:12 7:3, 5 10 20:17, Act.1:14, 1Co.9:5) may have been sons of Joseph and Mary (Mayor, Ja., Intr. viff.; DB, i, 320ff.) or of Joseph by a former marriage (Lft., Gal., 252ff.; DCG, i, 232ff.), but the view of Jerome, which makes ἀ. equivalent to ἀνεψιός, is inconsistent with Greek usage. (Cremer, 66.)\n(AS)","glosses":["brothers","brother","brother’s","of","sisters","some brothers"],"count":317,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"brothers"}},{"chapterId":"mat-1","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"brothers","kjv":"brethren"}},{"chapterId":"mat-4","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"brothers","kjv":"brethren"}},{"chapterId":"mat-4","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"brothers","kjv":"brethren"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"brother","kjv":"brother"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"brother","kjv":"brother"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"brother","kjv":"brother"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":47,"renderings":{"bsb":"brothers","kjv":"brethren"}},{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"brother’s","kjv":"brother's"}},{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"brother","kjv":"brother"}},{"chapterId":"mat-7","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"brother’s","kjv":"b